    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's a debate, but it feels like even the mainstream media and health orgs treat the 'freedom' arguments as if they're just excuses to avoid science. if a policy is objectively proven to save lives, isn't it kind of weird to treat the opposition as being on equal footing with the scientific consensus? shouldn't we distinguish between legitimate debate and just spreading misinformation?",
