      "content": "This tension between established consensus and principled dissent is a core characteristic of political debate, even in highly polarized topics.\n\nAdvocating for a strict \"misinformation vs. legitimate debate\" line is difficult because the *framing* of the argument is often ideological, not purely factual.\n\nMainstream discourse is often cautious to represent the \"opposition view,\" which in political terms is a necessary part of robust debate, but this can sometimes make the ideological *weight* of the arguments seem politically balanced, even when the scientific *certainty* is not.",
